        {
            "_id": "fvoGVahqBTTRtCqC",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg",
            "name": "Ground Slam",
            "sort": 700000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>The knucklehead slams the ground with an arm hand. The ground in a @Template[type:emanation|distance:10] becomes difficult terrain. If the knucklehead has a creature @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Grabbed] or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Restrained] in its arm hand, that creature takes @Damage[(2d10+10)[bludgeoning]|options:area-damage] damage. Other creatures in the area take @Damage[3d10[bludgeoning]|options:area-damage] damage with a basic @Check[reflex|dc:30|options:area-effect,inflicts:prone] save. A creature that fails the save also falls @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Prone].</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
